      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "Fuel names follow one scheme: §6N§r is natural, §6L§r, §6M§r and §6HE§r are low, medium and highly enriched, followed by the element and isotope - §6MEU§r is medium enriched uranium, §6HEP-239§r highly enriched plutonium-239.\n\nAll fuels start as billets. A §3ZIRNOX§r rod takes two billets, a §3PWR§r rod two billets around a polymer plate, an §3RBMK§r rod eight billets in an empty RBMK rod, and a §3Watz§r pellet four ingots around graphite. The tooltip of every rod shows its exact stats.\n\nSpent fuel comes out hot. Cool it in the Spent Fuel Pool Drum, then reprocess ZIRNOX, PWR and Watz fuel in the PUREX. Spent RBMK rods are taken apart into pellets for the SILEX. What you get back is the start of the next quest.",
